## About this licence, in plain words

RatNav is free. Use it, change it, fork it, share your fork — all fine, for anything that is not
about making money. What is not fine is selling it, charging for access to it, or building a paid
product on top of it.

## The name and the mark

**"RatNav" and the RatNav mark are not licensed to you.** The licence above covers the software.
Copyright licences do not grant rights in a name or a logo — PolyForm does not, and neither do MIT
or Apache — so this is a statement of what was never included rather than an extra restriction.

Concretely, without written permission you may not use "RatNav", or anything close enough to be
confused with it — "RatNav Plus", "RatNav Pro", "RatNav 2" — as the name of your own version, or
use the mark in `brand/` for anything other than referring to this project.

You are welcome to fork the code and say plainly that your version is based on RatNav. That is
accurate and there is no objection to it. What the name is for is telling people which one they are
downloading, and it stops doing that job the moment two different things answer to it.

Escape from Tarkov is a trademark of Battlestate Games. RatNav is an unofficial fan project with no
affiliation. RatNav uses data from community projects published under their own terms, credited in
the app and in the README; this licence covers RatNav and says nothing about theirs.

Battlestate Games set the rules for their own game and can change them whenever they like. RatNav
is built to stay well inside them — it reads files the game writes to your own disk and never
touches the game itself, which is set out in [docs/SAFETY.md](docs/SAFETY.md) — but no third party
can promise you what someone else will decide in future. You use RatNav at your own risk, and its
author is not liable for anything that follows from that, including action taken against a game
account.
